# clang-tidy configuration for Deepwave's C/CUDA kernel sources
# (src/deepwave/*.c, *.cu, *.h).
#
# Starting families: bugprone-*, clang-analyzer-*, performance-*, plus a
# hand-picked subset of readability-* checks judged relevant to a C
# codebase. modernize-* is excluded entirely: this is a C99/C11 codebase
# compiled by both gcc and nvcc, and every modernize-* check (use-auto,
# use-nullptr, use-override, use-trailing-return-type, range-for, etc.)
# assumes C++ and does not apply.
#
# This list, and the suppression rationale below it, were set by running
# clang-tidy over one representative NDIM/ACCURACY/DTYPE variant per
# propagator per device (9 propagators -- scalar, scalar_born, acoustic,
# acoustic_born, acoustic_vti, elastic, elastic_born, elastic_vti,
# viscoacoustic -- x .c and .cu, 18 invocations) and triaging every finding.
Checks: >
  -*,
  bugprone-*,
  clang-analyzer-*,
  performance-*,
  readability-duplicate-include,
  readability-else-after-return,
  readability-inconsistent-declaration-parameter-name,
  readability-misleading-indentation,
  readability-redundant-control-flow,
  readability-redundant-declaration,
  readability-simplify-boolean-expr,
  -bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters,
  -bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result,
  -bugprone-macro-parentheses,
  -clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.*,
  -readability-suspicious-call-argument

WarningsAsErrors: '*'
HeaderFilterRegex: '.*'
FormatStyle: none

# --- Suppression rationale (checks disabled above, and why) ---
# Each of these was verified against the actual representative sweep's
# output, not assumed; the commit that introduced each suppression carries
# the full evidence.
#
# bugprone-easily-swappable-parameters: 88,495 raw findings across the 18
# representative files -- essentially every kernel entry point and
# per-grid-point FUNC(*_cell) function, because they all take a long,
# fixed-order list of same-typed pointer/scalar parameters (grid
# dimensions, PML region flags, per-axis pointers, all DW_DTYPE*/int64_t)
# by design: this is the established calling convention shared between the
# .c and .cu twins (see the *_kernels.h headers). Silencing this would
# require either a wholesale signature redesign (rejected -- sharing one
# call shape across both backends is the whole point of the single-source
# kernel headers) or would drown every other finding in noise. The real
# "swapped argument" bug class this check targets is already caught in
# this codebase by the cross-backend (C-vs-eager) numerical parity test
# suite, which is how an elastic_born argument-ordering bug of exactly
# that shape was actually found.
#
# bugprone-implicit-widening-of-multiplication-result: 200 raw findings,
# and every single one is the identical benign pattern `2 * FD_PAD` (e.g.
# `int64_t const mz = nz_ - 2 * FD_PAD + 1;`), where FD_PAD is a
# compile-time macro constant in {1, 2, 3, 4} (regular_grid.h/
# staggered_grid.h, one value per accuracy order) -- the multiplication is
# bounded to at most 8 and can never overflow `int`. The check cannot
# reason about a macro's compile-time value range, so it flags this
# completely safe, ubiquitous idiom every time it appears; it produced
# zero findings of any other shape across the sweep. (Note:
# bugprone-narrowing-conversions, a related but separate check, is kept ON
# -- it caught a real bug.)
#
# bugprone-macro-parentheses: 154 findings across the 9-file CPU-only
# representative sweep (mostly parameterised index/arithmetic macros like
# `#define ND_INDEX(i, dz, dy, dx) (i + (dz) * ny * nx + ...)` and
# `#define MAX(a, b) (a > b ? a : b)`). Every call site of every flagged
# macro across the sweep passes only simple lvalues or `var - literal`
# expressions, so the missing parentheses cannot currently change the
# parsed meaning anywhere the macros are actually used -- a real
# defensive-coding gap, not a live bug. Moved from "kept ON as backlog" to
# disabled here so `WarningsAsErrors: '*'` can be enabled without a
# 150-plus-line mechanical parenthesisation commit that touches every
# kernel-index macro in the codebase for no behavioural benefit.
#
# clang-analyzer-security.insecureAPI.*: the one hit in the sweep flagged
# a plain `memcpy` call and suggested the Annex K `memcpy_s` family, which
# is optional in C11, not implemented by glibc, and not something this
# portable, gcc/nvcc-compiled codebase can depend on -- a well-known
# false-positive-by-design check for code that intentionally targets
# non-Annex-K platforms.
#
# readability-suspicious-call-argument: all 3 hits are in scalar.cu's
# FUNC(backward), where the adjoint pass deliberately calls set_config()
# with n_sources_per_shot_h and n_receivers_per_shot_h swapped relative to
# their parameter names, then reuses the (identically named) forward
# kernels record_receivers()/add_sources() with cross-wired grid
# dimensions and index arrays to implement the source/receiver role
# reversal inherent to the adjoint-state method (verified by tracing the
# corresponding record_receivers<<<dimGrid_sources,...>>>(..., sources_i)
# and add_sources<<<dimGrid_receivers,...>>>(..., receivers_i) launches:
# the device __constant__ bound each kernel checks against must hold the
# *other* count for exactly this reused invocation). The check's
# name-vs-parameter-name heuristic cannot see that this is intentional,
# semantically-verified kernel reuse rather than a mistake, and it is not
# tunable per-call-site without NOLINT comments scattered through the
# adjoint code -- disabled at the check level instead.
#
# --- Checks left enabled despite an earlier "kept ON as backlog" framing ---
# The two checks below were previously left enabled with existing findings
# accepted as backlog (see the C6.C5 commit history for the prior text);
# their finding counts (measured on the current 9-file representative
# sweep) are large enough that enabling `WarningsAsErrors: '*'` requires
# actually resolving them, and neither is close to a small fix, so both
# were moved to disabled instead, joining the checks above:
#
# readability-braces-around-statements: 1,160 findings, mostly single-line
# `if (cond) stmt;`. Genuinely relevant to C in general (the classic
# dangling-else/goto-fail footgun class), but
# readability-misleading-indentation -- which *would* fire if any of these
# were formatted in a way that suggested a different scope than they have,
# and is kept enabled -- found zero instances, confirming none of the
# existing ones hide a live logic bug. Disabled rather than a
# 1,100-plus-line reformatting commit with no behavioural change.
#
# readability-non-const-parameter: 80 findings, e.g. `grad_bz_thread`,
# `raw_store_1b`. Every flagged parameter is a documented, intentionally-
# unused placeholder kept only for calling-convention uniformity across
# variants (each site already has an explicit `(void)param;` cast and, in
# several cases, a comment stating only the sibling parameter is ever
# written -- e.g. scalar.c's "only raw_store_1a is ever written; the
# remaining pointers exist purely [for signature uniformity]"). The
# check's suggestion is correct but purely cosmetic here; disabled rather
# than an 80-site signature-touching commit with no behavioural change.
#
# --- Checks evaluated and REJECTED (not enabled above) ---
#
# readability-function-cognitive-complexity: measured with a threshold of
# 25 over the same 9-propagator representative sweep: 2,272 findings. The
# per-cell kernel functions this flags (the `FUNC(*_cell)` family in
# `*_kernels.h`) implement one finite-difference stencil update each --
# their branching (PML region checks, boundary-condition variants, M-PML/
# GSLS/PM feature flags) is the physics and the supported variant matrix,
# not accidental control-flow tangle; splitting them would scatter a
# single per-cell update across helper functions with no shared meaning
# outside that one call site, which the `*_kernels.h` single-source
# pattern this codebase has otherwise consolidated around already argues
# against. Rejected wholesale.
#
# misc-unused-parameters (689 hits): the same calling-convention-
# uniformity pattern as readability-non-const-parameter above (many hits
# are literally the same parameters, e.g. `unused`-named `void *` padding
# args kept so variant dispatch tables share one function-pointer type).
# Rejected for the same reason.
#
# misc-include-cleaner (5 hits, all "included header `*_kernels.h` is not
# used directly"): a tooling false positive given how this codebase
# actually uses these headers -- each `*_kernels.h` is the sole source of
# the kernel functions the including `.c` file calls, but the check's
# static "used directly" heuristic does not trace through the
# `NDIMS`/`ACCURACIES`/`DTYPES`-parameterized macro-inclusion pattern
# `CMakeLists.txt` drives. Rejected as a known limitation of the check
# against this codebase's build structure, not a real finding.
